Upstream ID3v2 hardening adapted to 1.13.1 and C++11.
Unlike newer TagLib, this zlib helper grows its output incrementally. Limit
that growth before allocation as well as checking declared output against
the upstream 64 MiB and 64:1 limits. Decode the declared length as big-endian
for ID3v2.3 and syncsafe for ID3v2.4 before applying those limits. Preserve
the old decompress entry point.
Retain the upstream inline test-size corrections. The pre-existing broken-
length test uses the release archive's compressed_id3_frame.mp3, identical
to compressed_id3_frame_invalid.mp3 in fa189f6c. Retain that commit's exact
142-byte picture assertion for the bounded output. No additional binary
fixtures or fixture-dependent tests are imported.
Upstream commits: https://github.com/taglib/taglib/commit/<full ID below>.

